```

This loops while there's a tie. The loop count depends on the actual die values. Since both real resolve and our trace use the SAME dice source (snapshot of same RNG), they should loop the same number of times and produce the same faces.

But wait - this loops on `tie` results. With `ties === "reroll"`, a tie on individual dice causes reroll. With `ties === "defender"`, no reroll needed.

Looking at `malpacoRules()`:
